  "summary_en": "New Zealand Ministry for Regulation guidance for regulatory leaders on adopting AI (predictive and generative) in regulatory practice. Covers governance, vendor procurement, workforce readiness, human-in-the-loop oversight, iterative low-risk piloting, ethics, Te Tiriti o Waitangi and Māori data, with a checklist. Accountability stays with human decision-makers.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Accountability remains with legally authorised decision-makers, not AI tools or vendors.",
   "Human-in-the-loop required at points of consequence, with guarding against automation bias and a right to appeal to a human.",
   "Start with small, reversible, low-risk pilots, possibly via regulatory sandboxes.",
   "Vendor contracts should include audit rights, data portability, exit plans and bias/performance commitments.",
   "Treat Māori data as taonga and consider Te Tiriti obligations early."
